WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
On the Home screen, click Open project… and pick the project.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The project opens on its graph, already computed: the status bar says all up to date and Run has nothing to run.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Click Show all, then fold the side panel.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Click the fold button of the side panel.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The whole graph: four rows, four workflows (S, H, O III, Stars), then the S-H-O combination, the Combine layers blocks and Post.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Open the Table view: one row per session.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Three sessions, one per filter: O III / H-alpha, O III / S II, and Stars for the night without a filter.

8
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Select a session card.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Open Block settings.

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.000
The session holds its lights and its own flat; darks and bias are one master shared by the sessions.

11
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Click Folded: one card per workflow.

12
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
S has 13 lights, H 10, O III 23 from two sessions, Stars 49; H, O III and Stars sit on the grid of S.

13
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Only S has an Astrometry block: it solves the field once, and the other rows take its grid.

14
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Right-click a Stacking block of H.

15
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Align on: the reference is S, and the method is Stars. The stars of the H stack are laid on those of S.

16
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Select the S-H-O block: its wires light up.

17
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.000
S-H-O is not a stack: it reads the starless images of S, H and O III.

18
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Open Block settings.

19
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Inputs: S and H feed the red pixels, O III the green and blue ones. Each filter gets a hue.

20
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Select the Combine layers block after S-H-O.

21
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Open Block settings.

22
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:46.000
The stars put back come from O III, not from the Stars night.

23
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Select the lower Combine layers block.

24
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Open Block settings.

25
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
The Stars workflow stays in the graph, computed, with its own Combine layers.

26
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Click Post.

27
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Post shows the finished image, version Palette and finish. Nothing is changed here.

28
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Open the File menu.

29
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Click New project.

30
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Click From template.

31
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:27.000
In the Color tab, Dual-band x2 is the template for a colour camera with two dual-band filters and a session for the stars.

32
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Click Dual-band x2.

33
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:38.000
The template brings the graph, the sessions named per filter and Align on on the grid of S. The frames are still to add.

34
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.000
Open the Table view of the new project.

35
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:49.000
The sessions are named per filter, and H, O III and Stars are already on the grid of S. The cells for the frames are empty.
